# ugv_sensor_sync

Sensor adapter and fusion package.

For full pull/build/launch instructions, use the consolidated runbooks:

- English: `ros2_ws/JETSON_BRINGUP_CHECKLIST.md`
- Chinese: `ros2_ws/JETSON_BRINGUP_CHECKLIST_ZH.md`

## Responsibilities

This package owns the stable middle layer between raw hardware topics and
navigation.

It provides:

- `zed_sync_node`: ZED depth/image/IMU adapter
- `lidar_sync_node`: timestamp-corrected LiDAR scan republisher
- `fusion_node`: LiDAR/ZED/encoder/optional-YOLO fusion into `/sensors/nav_frame`
- `debug_status_node`: compact one-line system status
- `bench_goal_node` and `mock_field_map_node`: test helpers

## Main Outputs

- `/sensors/nav_frame`: navigation contract
- `/sensors/synced`: richer debug bundle
- `/sensors/synced_summary`: JSON sensor/fusion health
- `/sensors/zed_obstacle_points`: ground-filtered ZED depth obstacle points, plus optional semantic points after fusion
- `/sensors/front_clearance_m`
- `/sensors/near_obstacle`
- `/zed/status`
- `/ugv/debug_status`

## Design Rules

- Raw sensor handling stays in adapter nodes.
- Cross-sensor timing and obstacle projection stay in `fusion_node`.
- Navigation should read `/sensors/nav_frame`, not raw ZED/LiDAR/encoder topics.
- Optional sensors should first be merged inside fusion before changing the navigation contract.

## ZED Depth Obstacle Filter

`fusion_node` estimates a per-row floor/background model and keeps connected
vertical clusters that stand closer than that model. This helps the low-mounted
ZED ignore visible floor while still detecting cones, buckets, boxes, and
chair/table legs.
